    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Tyler Soderstrom** leads the charge with an elite 71.98 score. His matchup against Kumar Rocker is a prime spot; a favorable park factor combined with a solid platoon advantage and a premium #2 spot in the order maximizes his efficiency. **Mickey Moniak** follows closely at 69.71, buoyed by a 14% dynamic platoon boost and wind blowing out at his venue, mitigating the risk posed by the catcher\u2019s arm. Meanwhile, **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start at 69.44, providing our most reliable floor for steals even without a defined opposing starter, as his elite profile continues to anchor the outfield.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the lineup was keeping **Cole Young** on the bench. Despite his 47.95 score and a projectable #2 spot, he fell just short of the efficiency threshold when compared to the high-upside platoons of **Austin Riley** and **Jose Caballero**. While **Jose Caballero** faces a tough arm in Shane Bieber, the 19% SP skill adjustment makes him a high-reward play despite the negative platoon regression. We remain cautious with **Brice Turang**, whose 56.66 score is heavily reliant on wind support; his steal potential is somewhat capped by a difficult matchup against Yoshinobu Yamamoto. As we await official confirmation on lineups for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Isaac Paredes**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Max Muncy**, **Brice Turang**, **Austin Riley**, **Seiya Suzuki**, **Jose Caballero**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Mickey Moniak**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Josh Naylor**, we are prepared to adjust if any late-scratch risks arise. We continue to monitor **James Wood** and **Giancarlo Stanton** on the IL, alongside rostered depth pieces **Trevor Story**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Henry Bolte** for potential spot starts.",
